--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATA — CREATIVE COMMONS ATTRIBUTION-NONCOMMERCIAL 4.0 INTERNATIONAL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Everything under data/ — the 13,515 medium records, the catalogue, the browser payloads,
the API exports and anything built from them — is licensed CC BY-NC 4.0.

  Attribute: MediaDB (github.com/omidard/Media), and the primary publication recorded in
  each record's `provenance.citation` for every medium you use.

  Non-commercial: the licence does not permit commercial use. For commercial use, obtain
  permission from the rights-holder of the upstream source named in that record's
  `provenance.source_name`; see NOTICE for who that is.

One licence covers the whole compilation because a compilation cannot grant more than its
most restrictive input allows. The upstream mix includes CC BY-NC material (FooDB, HMDB,
BMDB) and material that grants no reuse right at all: the 471 MediaDB records carry
"(c) 2014, Institute for Systems Biology, All Rights Reserved", and redistribution
permission has not been obtained. CC BY-NC 4.0 is therefore the strongest licence this
corpus can carry as a whole, and it also satisfies the attribution the CC BY sources are
owed.

There is no per-record licence field and no commercial-use flag. Which source a record
came from stays on the record as `provenance.source_id` and `provenance.source_name`, and
NOTICE names every source and the terms its material was taken under.

Nothing in this file is legal advice, and none of these labels is a warranty. NOTICE
records where each upstream statement of terms was read from and on what date, so you can
re-verify any of them yourself.


